    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30493" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Naucrătis</span></b> , is,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ναύκρατις</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town of the Delta in
				Egypt</i>, now <i>Salhadschar</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 10,
				11, § 64</span></i>; <i><span class="en">31, 10, 46, §
			111</span></i>.— Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Naucrătītes</span></b> , ae, m.
			<i>adj., of Naucratis, Naucratian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 9, 9, § 49</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Naucrătĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., 
			<i>Naucratian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ostium Nili,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 10, 11, § 64</span></i>
			.</div>
